Installation Instructions
*************************

libeflvala uses Meson (https://mesonbuild.com) as its canonical build system.

Prerequisites:
  - meson >= 0.61.0
  - ninja
  - valac (Vala compiler)
  - pkg-config
  - EFL development libraries (eina, evas, ecore, edje, elementary),
    version >= 1.27 (the bindings target the EFL 1.27 API)
  - libgee development files (gee-0.8)
  - glib-2.0 / gobject-2.0 development files (>= 2.18)

Basic Installation
==================

  1. Configure the build directory:

       meson setup build

     Add options as needed, e.g.:

       meson setup build --prefix=/usr/local -Dlibrary=false -Dexamples=false -Dtests=false

  2. Compile:

       meson compile -C build

  3. Run the test suite (optional):

       meson test -C build --print-errorlogs

  4. Install:

       meson install -C build

     Staged installs are supported via DESTDIR:

       DESTDIR=/path/to/stage meson install -C build

Build Options
=============

  -Dlibrary=false   Skip building the eflvala convenience library (default: true)
  -Dexamples=false  Skip building example applications        (default: true)
  -Dtests=false     Skip building test programs               (default: true)

Run `meson configure build` to list all standard and project options.

Uninstalling
============

  meson uninstall -C build
